  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 247 AM EDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nHappy Halloween. \n\nAn unrelated note: daylight savings time ends tonight.\n\nHigh pressure is crossing lower MI early this morning, moving\nslowly ese-ward. Some areas of low lake effect cloud cover \nlinger over eastern upper and far ne lower MI. Thin cirrus is \nalso encroaching on southern areas. A chilly morning, but to\nthis point little in the way of fog.\n\nTrailing behind the surface high, a 500mb shortwave ridge over \nthe northern plains will be moving over our heads Sunday\nafternoon. Some troffing is butting into the ridge axis by then,\nimmediately trailing it. There are some convective-looking\nelements on radar and satellite to our w, from WI westward.\nSteepening mid-level lapse rates will attempt to generate some\nlight showers, though mostly just result in virga here. Still,\na few showers are possible after midnight tonight into Sunday \nmorning. This should provide minimal interruption to Halloween \nplans.\n\nOtherwise quiet Sunday afternoon into Monday morning. Models are\na little faster today in starting to erode heights aloft later\nMonday, in face of a strengthening low level jet and associated\ntheta-e advection. A chance of showers could reach nw lower MI\nas soon as Monday afternoon. This is in advance of an evolving \nupper low and strung-out surface low in the plains and \neventually MS Valley. Likely to categorical pops Monday night \ninto early Wednesday, with multiple rounds of showers expected. \nNo thunder currently, but some respectable rainfall regardless. \n\nWith at least some sporadic stream interactions next week, the \nforecast gets less certain midweek and beyond. ECMWF is much \nwetter, as low pressure now passes a bit to our south late in \nthe week. Others have a weaker system ejecting to our north, \nwith smaller precip chances. \n\nTemps will remain above normal. We will be warming from today to\nabout Tuesday, then likely gradually cooling again after that.",
